    "substitutions": [
      "Compile only authenticated method AST nodes; never import or execute the original module, class, initializer, or external methods.",
      "Synthetic getters supply one shared complete book and explicit identical carry per venue. Source depth is at least base_book_quantity; original get_symbol_price book acquisition and shallow-book behavior are not authenticated.",
      "Capacity getters are normalized stubs, not copied callees. BFX duration=1 tuple is physical BUY/SELL; MT5 duration=-1 tuple is physical SELL/BUY. Existing legacy_margin_vectors.json authenticates the dynamic callee separately.",
      "Synthetic config supplies all max/min limits, keep_last_trader=false, and memory-only set; logger is synthetic, asyncio.gather is real, sleep is a no-op.",
      "FX is a migration input mapping only: original MT5 caller prices are current USD bid*FX bid and ask*FX ask, computed before float conversion. No original FX callee is authenticated.",
      "Caller local-result observation captures real_profit_rate_long/short from the exact authenticated calculation code object's return frame, restoring the previous trace in finally.",
      "Taker candidate and risk result are separate original outputs; a rejected SHORT candidate does not fall back to LONG."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "Explicit valid values only; no legacy missing-field, invalid-input, account production, live admission, last-account rotation, or multi-account live support claim.",
      "Maker base_price/amount/spread/lev and selected identities are authenticated caller outputs. Final multiplicative price, passive clamp, and leverage minimum one are separate Owner-frozen migration contracts, tested elsewhere.",
      "Bitfinex same-rate carry inputs do not authenticate the margin_funding producer or realized cash flow."
    ],
    "encoding": "All scalar input/output numbers are decimal strings preserving original float repr; per-case input replaces whole top-level default fields.",
    "numeric_comparison": "Identity, direction, candidate existence, and risk bool compare exactly. Only numeric outputs use absolute 1e-12; no tolerance changes branching.",
    "absolute_tolerance": "0.000000000001",
    "strict_boundaries": "Both direction boundary prices use the binary-exact ratio 144/128, yielding 0.125; thresholds use math.nextafter(0.125,-inf), 0.125, math.nextafter(0.125,+inf).",
    "case_count": 59,
    "expected_outputs_sha256": "bb12dd4872ed170b972d45fa9708059644830a6f5528eaf6924500fd592a1273"
  },
